  "id": "intraocular-pressure",
  "term": "intraocular pressure",
  "definition": "Intraocular pressure is the pressure inside the eye. In the source material, it is described as becoming excessive when the production of aqueous humor and its drainage out of the eye are out of balance, and this excess pressure is a common cause of glaucoma.",
